; Storage on a double-density diskette, for an `atari/800xl.ngp` program whose
; Container is the `.atr`: the diskette's sectors, the driver that reads them
; and the decoders the tool ships. A Project includes this beside the machine.
;
; The sectors from the fourth: the boot record has the first three and the load
; image whatever is left after the storage a program uses. A unit is 256
; sectors, which is the one size the `.atr` takes, and three of them reach past
; the 180 KB a double-density diskette holds. It is a ceiling and not a
; reservation: what the image costs is what the program's Payloads came to.
storage { units 3 size 65536 }

; Every Transition calls the driver and the decoders, so they are resident. The
; OS the driver calls into is resident already; a decoder nothing uses is
; dropped.
modules { "atari/disk.asm"  "stream/zx0.asm" }
resident { disk, zx0 }
